WebKit: the PlayStation page types text and runs editing commands for keys.

WebPage::handleEditingKeyboardEvent is the hook through which WebCore's keyboard event default
handling reaches the editor: a key down runs the editing command its key stands for (arrows,
Home, End, Delete, Backspace, select all, copy, cut, paste, undo) and a key press inserts its
text. The GTK and WPE ports leave it to a toolkit input method, and the PlayStation port's
version is `notImplemented()`, so a UI process that forwards key events through WebKit's C API
(WKPageHandleKeyboardEvent) got keydown, keypress and keyup events in the page but no text in
any field. This is the table and the three-step flow of the Windows port, written for WebCore's
current editor API.

--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/playstation/WebPagePlayStation.cpp
